title: The Beginning of Wisdom – Wisdom and the Fear of the LORD
description: Wisdom and the fear of the LORD: God's wisdom, not man's; the righteous and the wicked; the tongue; wisdom and the strange woman; and true riches, from the teachings on Proverbs and the wisdom that leads to Christ.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-wisdom.html
highlight: wis

# One deck for the topic "Wisdom & the fear of the LORD" (77 teachings), its themes given equal weight.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.
# Fixed: "walk in the canal" -> "walk in the carnal" (16981), "stuff at the simplicity" -> "scoff at" (3628).

=== Introduction
--- The Beginning of Wisdom [title]
overline: Doctrine · Wisdom & the fear of the LORD
heading: The Beginning of Wisdom
sub: Proverbs and the wisdom that leads to Christ.
refs: Proverbs 9:10; Proverbs 3:5-6; Colossians 2:3; Ecclesiastes 12:13
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 17142
--- The fear of the Lord
big: Proverbs 1:7 | mark: The fear of the LORD is the beginning of knowledge
p: It is astounding how we, as men, can hear God's word, know His word, study it, hear it preached, and yet still lean on our own understanding.
p: God's word should lead us to fear Him. To respect His holiness, power, mercy and justice. His wrath and His judgments. This is what makes a man wise. And it is every parent's responsibility to teach it to our children. It is the greatest inheritance we can give them ([[Proverbs 1:8-9]]).
read: app:doctrine-wisdom~17142 | The fear of the Lord the beginning of knowledge

=== God's wisdom, not man's
# from 17153
--- Lean not unto thine own understanding
kicker: God's wisdom, not man's
big: Proverbs 3:5-6 | mark: lean not unto thine own understanding; he shall direct thy paths
p: This is the key verse of Proverbs. The foundational understanding. Remember it, sing it, say it. And in everything acknowledge God first.
p: Don't think to blaze your own trails and beat down your own paths. There is nothing new under the Sun and God's ways are the best ways. The old paths, tried and true.

# from 17219, 17202, 17256, 17215
--- A way that seemeth right
kicker: God's wisdom, not man's
big: Proverbs 14:12 | mark: There is a way which seemeth right unto a man, but the end thereof are the ways of death
p: Man is able to rationalize any transgression, every petty sin and idle thought. But man's ways are not God's ([[Isaiah 55:8-9]]).
p: *Every way of a man is right in his own eyes: but the LORD pondereth the hearts* ([[Proverbs 21:2]]). Often we can do the right things for the wrong reasons. A man can do good for bad reasons, he can do evil with good intentions. God knows our hearts.

# from 16980, 16981, 17192
--- Jesus, the vein of wisdom
kicker: God's wisdom, not man's
big: Colossians 2:3 | mark: In whom are hid all the treasures of wisdom and knowledge
p: Job describes the relative ease of finding silver and gold, compared to the wisdom of God ([[Job 28:12-13]]). In Christ is all God's wisdom and knowledge. Jesus is the vein of wisdom, through the fear of God.
p: *But we have the mind of Christ* ([[1 Corinthians 2:16]]). But our flesh is at enmity with the spirit, and so when we walk in the carnal, we have less access to the wisdom of God. The root of the righteous, that is Christ Jesus, shall not be moved ([[Proverbs 12:3]]). All wisdom leads to Christ.

# from 17523, 3628, 8826
--- The foolishness of God
kicker: God's wisdom, not man's
big: 1 Corinthians 1:18 | mark: the preaching of the cross is to them that perish foolishness
p: Despite all his knowledge and wisdom, Solomon recognized the ways of God are still far above him ([[Ecclesiastes 8:17]]). Not by man's wisdom. But by His Spirit.
p: We all know people today who are constantly looking for supernatural signs from God before they can commit to believing, or who seek to impose their own logic on matters that are spiritual, and who scoff at the simplicity of the Gospel. What many see as foolishness, or weakness, is actually the wisdom of God.

# from 16861, 3653, 3646
--- True things, false points
kicker: God's wisdom, not man's
big: Job 4:17 | mark: Shall mortal man be more just than God?
p: Eliphaz uses true things to make false points. Many times the greatest lies are based on a misrepresentation or misapplication of the greatest truths.
p: Just because you believe something about the world to be true, doesn't make it Biblical doctrine. Literal creation is a primary doctrine. The shape of the earth isn't Biblical doctrine. Don't project your opinions of the worldly onto scripture. Sons of Belial, Jews and reprobates being liars is true because the Bible tells us so; we don't have to prove they lie about the shape of the earth. If you think you know for certain anything other than Christ and him crucified, you're a fool ([[1 Corinthians 2:2]]).

# from 17544, 5020
--- The whole duty of man
kicker: God's wisdom, not man's
big: Ecclesiastes 12:13 | mark: Fear God, and keep his commandments: for this is the whole duty of man
p: Solomon the Wise comes to the ultimate conclusion that the purpose of life isn't gathering riches, or pleasure or mirth. It is only to fear God and keep His commandments.
p: *Turn not to the right hand nor to the left* ([[Proverbs 4:27]]). Don't get caught up in the false binary presented by the beast. The true third position is the path of righteousness and steadfast faith in God alone.
